            "heading": "1. Negative-Mass Cavity Method (Zero Integration!)",
            "headingHinglish": "1. Negative-Mass Cavity Method (Zero Integration!)",
            "body": "Agar mass M₁ wali poori symmetric body mein se mass M₂ ka cavity tukda (centre r₂ par) kaat liya jaye, toh bache hue hisse ko **(+M₁) + (-M₂)** ka superposition maano!\n- **Centre of Mass:**\n  ```\n    r_cm = (M₁ r₁ - M₂ r₂) / (M₁ - M₂)\n  ```\n- **Moment of Inertia (about ANY axis O):**\n  ```\n    I_remaining = I_whole(about O) - I_removed(about O)\n  ```\n  *(Dhyan: Dono MI exact SAME axis O ke about hone chahiye — cavity ke liye Parallel Axes Theorem lagana mat bhoolna!)*",
            "bodyHinglish": "Agar mass M₁ wali poori symmetric body mein se mass M₂ ka cavity tukda (centre r₂ par) kaat liya jaye, toh bache hue hisse ko **(+M₁) + (-M₂)** ka superposition maano!\n- **Centre of Mass:**\n  ```\n    r_cm = (M₁ r₁ - M₂ r₂) / (M₁ - M₂)\n  ```\n- **Moment of Inertia (about ANY axis O):**\n  ```\n    I_remaining = I_whole(about O) - I_removed(about O)\n  ```\n  *(Dhyan: Dono MI exact SAME axis O ke about hone chahiye — cavity ke liye Parallel Axes Theorem lagana mat bhoolna!)*"
