            "heading": "Story Time: Subhadra aur Piano Wire ka Tension",
            "headingHinglish": "Story Time: Subhadra aur Piano Wire ka Tension",
            "body": "**Subhadra** ek acoustic-materials engineer hai jo steel piano wires, railway tracks, aur concert halls mein sound speed test karti hai. Ek din usne ek steel wire ko tighten kiya (tension 4 guna badha diya) aur pulse bheja — pulse ki speed **double** ho gayi!\n\nPhir usne socha: *\"Steel mein sound 5000 m/s se bhaagta hai, paani mein 1500 m/s, aur hawa mein sirf 332 m/s! Aisa kyun? Aur jab 17th century mein Isaac Newton ne hawa mein sound ki speed calculate ki, toh unka answer 280 m/s kyun aaya jabki real speed 332 m/s hoti hai?\"*\n\nAaj hum har medium mein wave speed ka exact formula aur Newton–Laplace ki famous kahani seekhenge!",
            "bodyHinglish": "**Subhadra** ek acoustic-materials engineer hai jo steel piano wires, railway tracks, aur concert halls mein sound speed test karti hai. Ek din usne ek steel wire ko tighten kiya (tension 4 guna badha diya) aur pulse bheja — pulse ki speed **double** ho gayi!\n\nPhir usne socha: *\"Steel mein sound 5000 m/s se bhaagta hai, paani mein 1500 m/s, aur hawa mein sirf 332 m/s! Aisa kyun? Aur jab 17th century mein Isaac Newton ne hawa mein sound ki speed calculate ki, toh unka answer 280 m/s kyun aaya jabki real speed 332 m/s hoti hai?\"*\n\nAaj hum har medium mein wave speed ka exact formula aur Newton–Laplace ki famous kahani seekhenge!"
